ently there are 18 red pixels (2 red blocks). Let me check the current state and try to overlap with the remaining red blocks.", "kind": "reasoning", "inContext": false}, {"label": "ASSISTANT", "content": "World model: KEY FINDING: When white character overlaps a red block and SPACE is pressed, that red block is removed! Red pixels decreased from 27 to 18 after RIGHT, SPACE. Currently 18 red pixels (2 blocks) remain.\nGoal model: Overlap with remaining red blocks and press SPACE to remove them.\nAction model: Arrow keys move white character. SPACE removes overlapping red blocks.\nPlan: Check current state, move to overlap with remaining red blocks, press SPACE.", "kind": "reasoning", "inContext": true}, {"label": "TOOL CALL: python", "content": "<tool_call>\n<function=python>\n<parameter=code>\n# Check current state\nseg = current_frame.segmentation\nwhite = None\nreds = []\nfor n in seg['nodes']:\n    if n['color'] == 'W' and n['pixels'] > 50:\n        white = n\n    elif n['color'] == 'R':\n        reds.append(n)\n\nif white:\n    b = white['boundary']\n    min_r = min(p[0] for p in b)\n    max_r = max(p[0] for p in b)\n    min_c = min(p[1] for p in b)\n    max_c = max(p[1] for p in b)\n    print(f\"White: ({min_r},{min_c})-({max_r},{max_c})\")\n    for r in reds:\n        rb = r['boundary']\n        rmin_r = min(p[0] for p in rb)\n        rmax_r = max(p[0] for p in rb)\n        rmin_c = min(p[1] for p in rb)\n        rmax_c = max(p[1] for p in rb)\n        inside = (rmin_r >= min_r and rmax_r <= max_r and rmin_c >= min_c and rmax_c <= max_c)\n        print(f\"  Red: ({rmin_r},{rmin_c})-({rmax_r},{rmax_c}), inside={inside}\")\n\n# Try pressing SPACE to see if current overlap removes red blocks\nresult = action(['SPACE'])\nprint(f\"Level completed: {last_action_result.get('level_completed')}\")\nseg = current_frame.segmentation\nred_pixels = sum(n['pixels'] for n in seg['nodes'] if n['color'] == 'R')\nprint(f\"Red pixels after SPACE: {red_pixels}\")\nfor n in seg['